# Train Your AI Fighter & Pen Fight 3D — Repository Summary

## 1. Executive Summary

This repository hosts **"Train Your AI Fighter"**, an offline-first, browser-based combat simulation and Web3 game created for the Monad Hackathon. 

The core premise is autonomous, prompt-driven competition: two players describe their strategy in plain English (up to 200 words). The game compiles these descriptions in real time into combat attributes (`aggression`, `defense`, `speed`), and assigns them to autonomous AI agents that battle without human intervention. The victor's fighter profile and match metadata are queued for minting as an on-chain NFT on Monad Testnet.

The project features two distinct simulation modes sharing the same input and state pipeline:
1. **AI Fighter**: A 2D martial arts arena fighting game with procedural camera perspective ([`scene3d.js`](file:///C:/Users/Tanuj/Documents/Git-repos/gamingNft/js/scene3d.js)) and an optional full WebGL 3D renderer ([`render3d.js`](file:///C:/Users/Tanuj/Documents/Git-repos/gamingNft/js/render3d.js)).
2. **Pen Fight 3D**: A 3D simulation of the classic school desk pen duel ([`penfight.js`](file:///C:/Users/Tanuj/Documents/Git-repos/gamingNft/js/penfight.js), [`penfight3d.js`](file:///C:/Users/Tanuj/Documents/Git-repos/gamingNft/js/penfight3d.js)), driven by real rigid-body Newtonian mechanics in SI units.

The entire project operates with **zero build step and zero runtime network dependencies** (no npm, no bundler, no LLM API, no audio asset files, and no CDN scripts).

